From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] An API for a frontend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a JSON API for a frontend that runs on another origin (the Vite dev
server, localhost:5173).

- maago.API in the routes makes an API route. What the view returns is
  the JSON, and an error is an RFC 9457 problem
  (application/problem+json). The URL function comes from the name:
  api_posts is APIPostsURL. Initialisms such as API, URL and ID are all
  capitals, as Go has them
- The post list calls the same query as the board's page. No posts is
  []:

      func APIPosts(ctx context.Context, db maago.DB, in APIPostsIn) ([]PostSummary, error)

- Writing a post takes the same PostForm as HTML, as one JSON object
  ({"title": "…", "body": "…"}), with the same rules and texts. The view
  writes in the request's transaction like any POST view, and returns
  the post, not a page:

      func APICreatePost(ctx context.Context, tx maago.Tx, in NewPostIn) (Post, error)

  A form that breaks a rule never reaches the view: the generated code
  answers 422 with a list of errors. Broken JSON or an empty body is a
  400
- savePost(ctx, tx, …), shared with the HTML view, checks what only the
  database knows (the same title, an overlapping pin) and writes it on
  the form. It takes a maago.Tx: it writes, so only a view with a
  transaction can call it. The API view returns what it found as
  maago.Invalid(&f.Title, …) or maago.InvalidForm(…): the same 422
- Once written: 200 and the new post. The JSON keys are the Go field
  names (ID, Title), and numbers are numbers

Config.Origins in main lists the origins to trust. Such an origin:
- gets a 204 for the question asked first (preflight, OPTIONS)
- gets Access-Control-Allow-Origin on the real response, so its page
  reads it

A POST from an origin not listed is a 403 from the CSRF check. Its
preflight gets no permission (405, no allow headers), so the browser
does not send the real request.

diff --git a/board/urls.go b/board/urls.go
index e251613..b069f7d 100644
--- a/board/urls.go
+++ b/board/urls.go
@@ -17,4 +17,8 @@ var Routes = maago.Routes{
 	maago.POST("/posts/{id}/publish", "post_publish", Publish),
 	maago.POST("/posts/{id}/archive", "post_archive", Archive),
 	maago.POST("/posts/{id}/delete", "post_delete", HidePost),
+
+	// JSON for a frontend on another origin: main trusts it in Config.Origins.
+	maago.GET("/api/boards/{id}/posts", "api_posts", APIPosts, maago.API),
+	maago.POST("/api/boards/{id}/posts", "api_post_create", APICreatePost, maago.API),
 }
